-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",168,{
[5345]="70066937\n1\tRepair the small fishing net\tGwían has asked you to repair a small fishing net in Melgobas.\n2\tTalk to Gwían\tGwían wishes to talk to you. She can be found in Melgobas.\n3\tRepair the small fishing net... again\tYou seem to have missed a tear on the corner of the small fishing net. You can repair it in Melgobas.\n4\tTalk to Gwían\tGwían wishes to talk to you. She can be found in Melgobas.\n5\tRepair the other small fishing net\tGwían has asked you to repair another small fishing net in Melgobas.\n6\tTalk to Gwían\tGwían wishes to talk to you again. Perhaps she'll let you repair the larger net now...? She can be found in Melgobas.\n7\tRepair the large fishing net\tGwían has finally allowed you to repair the large fishing net. You can find it in Melgobas.\n8\tTalk to Gwían\tYou have finished repairing all of Gwían's fishing nets. You should talk to her in Melgobas.\n",
[5346]="7006EC42\n1\tFind a place to fish in the harbour\tPerhaps you could fish near the bridge in the harbour.\n2\tFish from the pier in the harbour\tThe pier near the bridge in the harbour looks good. You should fish here.\n3\tFind a place to fish at the west side of the harbour\tMaybe you should try fishing from the pier on the west side of the harbour.\n4\tFish off the pier in the west side of the harbour\tThe pier on the west side of the harbour looks great for fishing. Time to cast a line!\n5\tFind a place to fish near the waterfall above the harbour\tA waterfall flows from above into the harbour. Could there be fish up there?\n6\tCatch a fish near the waterfall above the harbour\tIt looks like there are indeed fish near the waterfall above the harbour. You should catch one.\n7\tFind a place to fish from the sandbar in the north\tThe sandbar on the north side of the island has great potential for a fishing spot. You should scout the location.\n8\tCatch a fish from the sandbar in the north\tThe sandbar on the north side of the island looks like a great fishing spot. You should catch fish there.\n9\tBring the fish back to Merkhâma\tThere are many great fishing spots all over the island. You should bring your catch to Merkhâma and tell her.\n",
[5347]="70040EEA\n1\tCatch fish off the wharf of Dol Amroth (total: 6)\tAn ideal fishing spot can be found on the low dock where the rowboats are tied up, south-east of Anírwen. You should fish on the low dock.\n2\tShow the fish to Anírwen\tAnírwen is at the market near the docks of Dol Amroth, on the eastern side of the city. You should bring the fresh catch to Anírwen.\n",
[5348]="70046C50\n1\tCatch silvery pout (total: 10)\tFish can be caught down at the Cape Docks. You should catch some fish at your leisure.\n2\tTalk to Haldil\tHaldil is down by the Cape Docks. You should speak to Haldil when you have a moment.\n",
[5349]="70066942\n1\tTake fish from the full fish crate\tRindur has given you an empty bucket to fill with fish. You can fill it up from the full fish crate in Melgobas.\n2\tYou have filled your bucket with fish. You should set the fish out to dry on drying racks around Melgobas.\t\n3\tTalk to Rindur\tYou have set all the fish out to dry on drying racks. You should let Rindur in Melgobas know.\n",
[5350]="70026B09\n1\tCatch Easy Fish (total: 10)\tEasy Fish can be caught at the Bywater Pond. The odds are good that you'll catch Easy Fish with every cast. Catch all the Easy Fish, if you can! But don't catch the Bad Fish, whatever you do....\n2\tCatch Simple Fish (total: 10)\tSimple Fish can be caught at the Bywater Pond. The odds are fairly good that you'll catch Simple Fish with every cast. Catch all the Simple Fish, if you can! But don't catch the Bad Fish, whatever you do....\n3\tCatch Possible Fish (total: 10)\tPossible Fish can be caught at the Bywater Pond. The odds are fair that you'll catch Possible Fish with every cast. Catch all the Possible Fish, if you can! But don't catch the Bad Fish, whatever you do....\n4\tCatch Tricky Fish (total: 10)\tTricky Fish can be caught at the Bywater Pond. The odds are somewhat fair that you'll catch Tricky Fish with every cast. Catch all the Tricky Fish, if you can! But don't catch the Bad Fish, whatever you do....\n5\tCatch Unlikely Fish (total: 10)\tUnlikely Fish can be caught at the Bywater Pond. Your odds of catching all the Unlikely Fish are, well...unlikely. Catch all the Unlikely Fish, if you can! But don't catch the Bad Fish, whatever you do....\n6\tShow Flobert Chubb what incredible luck you had\tFlobert Chubb can be found at the Fishing Pond in Bywater. You should return to Flobert Chubb at once.\n",
[5351]="7002EFA5\n1\tTalk to Burnoth to join the Riders Four in a raid against the Khundolar\tBurnoth is at the refugee camp outside Harwick. You should speak with Burnoth when you are ready to ride against the Easterlings.\n2\tTalk to Burnoth\tBurnoth is at the refugee camp outside Harwick. You should speak with Burnoth regarding the battle against the Easterlings.\n",
[5352]="70007800\n1\tDefeat Jasper Mudbottom\tJasper Mudbottom is at the brigand encampment at Ost Baranor, south of the Staddle farms. Falco Greenhand has asked you to put a stop to the Blackwold brigand, Jasper Mudbottom. He suggested you take friends.\n2\tTalk to Falco Greenhand at his farm\tFalco Greenhand is at his farm in Staddle, north of Ost Baranor. You should return to Falco Greenhand with news of your victory over Jasper Mudbottom.\n",
[5353]="70032BC4\n1\tSpeak with Reinn about his departure\tReinn is in the Twenty-first Hall. You should speak with Reinn.\n2\tUse the summoning horn to call Reinn when you are ready\tThe summoning horn can be found in the Twenty-first Hall, next to Mögr. You should use the horn to call Reinn to your side when you are ready to depart.\n3\tExplore the hall south of the Twenty-first Hall\tThe Great Hall of Durin is south of the Twenty-first Hall, found by taking a right from the southern arch. Mögr has asked you to explore the hall south of the Twenty-first Hall.\n4\tTalk to Reinn (use the horn to summon him)\tReinn can be called to your side using the horn he gave you. You should speak with Reinn.\n5\tExplore south-east in the Great Hall of Durin\tThe Great Hall of Durin is south of the Twenty-first Hall in Zelem-melek. You should explore the Great Hall of Durin in Zelem-melek with Reinn, heading south-east.\n6\tSpeak with Reinn (use the horn to summon him)\tReinn can be called to your side using the horn he gave you. You should speak with Reinn.\n7\tFind the owner of the camp-fire's light\tYou spotted the light of a camp-fire on the lower levels of the Great Hall of Durin. You should find the camp-fire and the one who tends it.\n8\tSpeak with Reinn (use the horn to summon him)\tReinn can be called to your side using the horn he gave you. You should speak with Reinn.\n",
[5354]="700276BC\n1\tTalk to the Rohirrim quartermaster\tThe quartermaster can be found in the Rohirrim camp at the Ford of Isen. Grimbold subtly inferred a plan to allow Daervunn to escape, but you will have to obtain some of the strong ale favoured by the Men of Rohan.\n2\tRecover ale-casks (total: 6)\tThe Dunlendings have a camp not too far from the Ford of Isen, where the stolen ale is being kept. You will need to fight your way into the Dunlending camp and retrieve the stolen casks if you want to enact Grimbold's plan to secretly release Daervunn.\n3\tBring the ale-casks to the quartermaster at the Ford of Isen\tThe Rohirrim quartermaster is at the Ford of Isen. You should return the ale-casks that you recovered to the quartermaster at Grimbold's encampment.\n",
[5355]="7000887E\n1\tReturn to Quartermaster Cynwiss at Tol Ascarnen\030Collect Thistledown-hides (total: 10)\tThistledown-aurochs can be found throughout the Ettenmoors. Quartermaster Cynwiss asked you to assist her in collecting hides to craft the flags of the Free Peoples in the Ettenmoors.\n",
[5356]="70017B87\n1\tTalk to Geirfast at the Twenty-first Hall\tGeirfast is in the Twenty-first Hall. You should speak with Geirfast again when you are prepared to travel to the strange cave.\n2\tTalk to Geirfast at the Twenty-first Hall\tGeirfast is at the Twenty-first Hall. You should return to Geirfast and tell him of the strange map you saw projected on the wall by the light of the torch.\n",
[5357]="7004E72B\n1\tDefeat dragon-kind on the path to Stormwall (total: 10)\030Examine the slain hart\030Examine the slain bear\030Examine the slain wolf\tYou should defeat dragon-kind on the path to Stormwall, which lies north-east of Skarháld.\n2\tSearch for the entrance to Stormwall\tYou should search for the entrance to Stormwall, high in the mountains north-east of Skarháld.\n3\tDefeat foes in Stormwall (total: 10)\030Find the source of all these beasts within Stormwall\tStormwall lies high in the mountains northeast of Skarháld. You should defeat enemies in Stormwall and find the source of all these beasts.\n4\tExamine the spider corpse\tStormwall lies high in the mountains north-east of Skarháld. You should examine the spider corpse you found in Stormwall.\n",
[5358]="70037AD9\n1\tDefeat the war machine assaulting the main gate\tThe gate along the road must not fall to the flames of Saruman's twisted machine. The gates must be defended until the deadly construct can be disabled and destroyed. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[5359]="7003A4A7\n1\tDefeat the war-machines assaulting the centre of the dike ([see journal]/3)\tThe gate along the road must not fall to the flames of Saruman's twisted machines. The gates must be defended until the deadly constructs can be disabled and destroyed. Protect the archers upon the dike and supply them with arrows so that they may defeat the foul constructs. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[5360]="7004309A\n1\tDefeat Haradrim scouts (total: 8)\030Collect piles of chopped wood (total: 8)\tHaradrim and chopped wood can be found among the trees to the south of Glaniath in Upper Lebennin. Arvellon has asked you to recover wood and defeat any Haradrim scouts that have passed into Upper Lebennin.\n2\tDeliver the wood to Arvellon in Glaniath\tArvellon can be found in Glaniath to the north-east of Pelargir. You have defeated many scouts and recovered a substantial amount of wood. You should now return to Arvellon.\n",
[5361]="70045FE4\n1\tSpeak with Rathon\tRathon can be found in the northern end of the First Circle of Minas Tirith You should speak with Rathon.\n2\tCollect bags of sand (total: 4)\tBags of sand can be found in the area of Minas Tirith surrounding Rathon. You should collect bags of sand for use in extinguishing the flames.\n3\tExtinguish fires in Minas Tirith (total: 4)\tStray fires can be found in the northern end of the First Circle of Minas Tirith. You should use the bags of sand to extinguish the flames.\n4\tSpeak with Húrin\tHúrin can be found outside the gates to Minas Tirith. You should report back to Húrin.\n",
[5362]="7004185A\n1\tTalk to the Steward in Ost Anglebed\tThe Steward can likely be found in his hall in Ost Anglebed. Barchir has asked you to travel east to Ost Anglebed and aid the men there in holding against the Enemy's forces.\n",
[5363]="70000150\n1\tDestroy the stolen fireworks\tThe brigand encampment is at Narrowcleeve, the heights in the south-west part of the Marish, not far from Woodhall. You can enter the camp by crossing a ford near the brink of a waterfall. Shirriff Robin Smallburrow sent you to speak with Paladin Took, the Thain of the Shire, about Hyacinth's stolen fireworks. The Thain suggested that they may have been stolen by a band of ruffians camped in the Marish and sent you to destroy the fireworks.\n2\tTalk to Thain Paladin Took II\tThe Thain is at the Great Smials in Tuckborough. The Thain, Paladin Took, sent you to destroy Hyacinth Took's stolen fireworks at a brigand encampment. With victory in hand, you should return to the Thain at once.\n",
[5364]="70026168\n1\tSpeak with Tanathron\tTanathron is in Duillond, near the ovens and the Boot-maker. You should speak with Tanathron about procuring flax fibre for linen shrew-stomping boots.\n2\tCollect flax plants (total: 8)\tFlax grows in the grasses along the road to Celondim that leads south from Duillond. You should collect stalks of flax so that Tanathron's precarious supply can remain perfectly balanced.\n3\tBring the flax plants to Tanathron and collect the fibres\tTanathron, the weaver, is in Duillond near the ovens. You should bring the flax plants to Tanathron to refurbish his dwindling supply.\n4\tBring the flax fibres to Deluraw\tDeluraw stands near the ovens in Duillond. You should bring the desired flax fibres to Deluraw, for they are apparently very difficult to come by.\n",
[5365]="700088B7\n1\tSlaughter members of the Coldfells Army (total: 10)\tDefenders of the Free Peoples can be found throughout the Ettenmoors. Soldier Fandmau directed you to slaughter the defenders loyal to the Free Peoples.\n2\tReturn to Soldier Fandmau at Tírith Rhaw\tSoldier Fandmau is at Tírith Rhaw. You found and slaughtered a good number of the enemy.\n",
[5366]="7001AF9B\n1\tDead Man's Perch lies between the northern and southern Barrow-downs. Sal Haywood asked you to search the Dead Man's Perch for the other guides out of Bree.\t\n",
[5367]="70019D40\n1\tFind the flet-runner on Telain Glorelloth\tYou are seeking the flet-runner on Telain Glorelloth. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tTalk to the flet-runner on Telain Glorelloth\tThe flet-runner on Telain Glorelloth is waiting to speak with you.\n",
[5368]="70019D3F\n1\tFind the flet-runner on the large high flet belonging to Telain Neduil\tYou are seeking the flet-runner on a large, high flet of Telain Neduil. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tTalk to the flet-runner on Telain Neduil\tThe flet-runner on Telain Neduil is waiting to speak with you.\n",
[5369]="70019D3E\n1\tFind the flet-runner by the Stable-master\tThe flet-runner you are seeking is by the Caras Galadhon Stable-master. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tTalk to the flet-runner by the Stable-master\tThe flet-runner by the Stable-master is waiting to speak with you.\n",
[5370]="70019D41\n1\tFind the flet-runner outside the House of Celeborn\tYou are seeking the flet-runner outside the House of Celeborn. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tTalk to the flet-runner outside the House of Celeborn\tThe flet-runner outside the House of Celeborn is waiting to speak with you.\n",
[5371]="70070D00\n1\tDefeat drone corpse-flies (total: 8)\030Defeat warrior corpse-flies (total: 8)\tYour mission is to travel to Saig Hathíl and thin the numbers of the sickle-flies there who have become dangerous and aggressive.\n2\tDefeat the enraged hive-matron\tYour mission is to travel to Saig Hathíl and thin the numbers of the sickle-flies there who have become dangerous and aggressive.\n",
[5372]="7005B22C\n1\tTalk to Shúkurz near Vatug-ronk\tShúkurz will meet you by the southern entrance of Vatug-ronk. Vatug-ronk is located on the lowest level of Deepscrave, to the west of Aslíf.\n2\tUnlock cages (total: 2)\tShúkurz has asked you to free a few imprisoned Orcs. Their cages can be found around Vatug-ronk.\n3\tTalk to Shúkurz near Vatug-ronk\tYou have freed the Orcs. Shúkurz is waiting for you by the southern entrance to Vatug-ronk.\n",
[5373]="7000E8B7\n1\tDefeat Jabe Grimshaw\tThe Rangers believe Jabe Grimshaw can be found in the ruins of Barad Rath in Evendim, far to the west of Esteldín. Handarod has asked you to seek out the brigand Jabe Grimshaw and defeat him.\n2\tTalk to Handarod\tHandarod is at Esteldín in the North Downs, far to the east of Evendim. You should return to Handarod and tell him of Jabe Grimshaw's defeat.\n",
[5374]="7005C8B1\n1\tTravel to Grúmachath with Múta\tGrúmachath can be found to the north-east of the Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate. After escaping with your aid, Múta intends to join the Zhélruka expedition at Grúmachath. You should travel to Grúmachath with Múta. NOTE: If you become separated from Múta, use the horn she gave you to summon her to your side.\n2\tTalk to Múta\tMúta can be found at your side. You have arrived at Grúmachath. You should talk to Múta. NOTE: If you become separated from Múta, use the horn she gave you to summon her to your side.\n3\tJoin Múta by the camp-fire at the centre of Grúmachath\tMúta can be found at Grúmachath. After arriving at Grúmachath, Múta ran off toward the centre of the encampment. You should join Múta by the camp-fire at Grúmachath.\n4\tTalk to Múta at Grúmachath\tMúta can be found at Grúmachath. You have found Múta speaking to the Zhélruka in charge of Grúmachath. You should talk to Múta.\n5\tTalk to Mézto at Grúmachath\tMézto can be found at Grúmachath. You have found Múta speaking to the Zhélruka in charge of Grúmachath, Mézto. You should talk to Mézto.\n",
[5375]="7003332A\n1\tDefeat the Easterlings in the clearing\tThe people of Dale are attempting to flee to the safety of the Lonely Mountain. The Easterling army is not far behind...\n2\tDefend the clearing from the Easterling assault\tThe people of Dale are attempting to flee to the safety of the Lonely Mountain. The Easterling army is not far behind...\n",
[5376]="7003332B\n1\tDefeat the Easterlings in the clearing\tThe people of Dale are attempting to flee to the safety of the Lonely Mountain. The Easterling army is not far behind...\n2\tDefend the clearing from the Easterling assault\tThe people of Dale are attempting to flee to the safety of the Lonely Mountain. The Easterling army is not far behind...\n",
